# Freshservice status

Keep status honest. Prefer a connected Freshservice / ITSM MCP when one is
ready. If none is connected, use the operator’s configured API or UI path —
do not invent tool names, workspace ids, or credentials.

## Lifecycle

| Moment | Status posture |
| --- | --- |
| Just created, no start directive | Leave Open / default created |
| Waiting on requester / vendor | Pending (say what is waiting) |
| Work actively underway | In Progress / Open with assignee when set |
| Ask completed with evidence | Resolved |
| Confirmed closed / no further action | Closed |

Exact status labels vary by workspace — use the workspace’s real status names
from the ticket or tools; do not invent a custom workflow.

## Honesty gates

- Do **not** mark **Resolved** / **Closed** without evidence the requested
  outcome is done (or the requester confirmed).
- Pending ≠ resolved. Say what is waiting (user reply, vendor, change window,
  approval).
- Never invent priority, group, or assignee — only set values the user named
  or the ticket already has.
- Do not “resolve” because chat feels finished or a PR was opened without
  verification.

## Assignment and priority

1. Assign only when the user named a group/agent or host config supplies one.
2. Priority / urgency / impact: set only from named values or existing ticket
   fields; do not escalate for drama.
3. Reassignment: state from → to; refuse silent broad reassignment of many
   tickets unless the user listed them.

## Transitions

1. Read the current ticket (id known) before changing status.
2. Apply the smallest honest move that matches the user’s verb.
3. If a transition fails, report the blocker — do not fake status in chat.
4. After mutate: return ticket id, new status, and evidence (not secret dumps).

## Scope

- Do not invent a ticket so this status rule can run.
- Naming a ticket id authorizes status work on that ticket when the user asked
  to update/resolve/assign — it does not authorize create of a new one.
- Create-only turns leave status alone unless the user also asked to board /
  assign / resolve (see `freshservice-create`).
